==English==
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|matrone|lang=fro}}, {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|matrona|lang=la||married woman}}, from {{term|mater|lang=la||mother}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/meɪtrən/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪtrən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A mature woman; a wife or a widow, especially, one who has borne children; a woman of staid or motherly manners.
#* [[w:Shakespeare|Shakespeare]]
#*: ''Your wives, your daughters, Your '''matrons''', and your maids.
# A housekeeper; especially, a woman who manages the domestic economy of a public institution; a head nurse in a hospital; as, the matron of a school or hospital.

